From: mochiOS <dev@mochios.local>
Subject: [PATCH] x86/mboot: poll idle control rings after one scheduler tick

The control ring carries synchronous display and input requests. Sleeping
10 ms after finding it empty adds that delay to the next arriving request.
Sleep for one tick (1 ms with the board configuration), without busy polling
or blocking the vCPU while other Linux tasks have work to do.

--- a/arch/x86/kernel/cpu/mboot.c
+++ b/arch/x86/kernel/cpu/mboot.c
@@ -4016,7 +4016,7 @@ static int mboot_control_worker(void *unused)
 			break;
 		}
 		if (result == MBOOT_EVENT_NO_EVENT)
-			msleep_interruptible(10);
+			schedule_timeout_interruptible(1);
 		else
 			cond_resched();
 	}
